<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Autoencoder</title><link>https://jaehun.me/tags/autoencoder/</link><description>딥러닝 컴파일러 엔지니어 류재훈의 기술 블로그. LLM 추론 최적화, KV 캐시, 컴파일러, C++와 AI 논문·오픈소스 코드 분석을 정리합니다.</description><language>ko-kr</language><atom:link href="https://jaehun.me/tags/autoencoder/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>[논문리뷰]: Continuous Autoregressive Language Models</title><link>https://jaehun.me/posts/%EB%85%BC%EB%AC%B8%EB%A6%AC%EB%B7%B0-continuous-autoregressive-language-models/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://jaehun.me/posts/%EB%85%BC%EB%AC%B8%EB%A6%AC%EB%B7%B0-continuous-autoregressive-language-models/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 26 Dec 2025 00:00:00 +0900</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a&#10; href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.27688v1"target="_blank"&#10; class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"&#10; &gt;논문 링크&lt;svg class="h-3 w-3 flex-shrink-0" id="external-link" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24"&gt;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 3h6v6m-11 5L21 3m-3 10v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="calm-토큰-by-토큰-병목을-연속-벡터-by-벡터로-우회하는-likelihood-free-언어모델링"&gt;CALM: 토큰-by-토큰 병목을 “연속 벡터-by-벡터”로 우회하는 Likelihood-Free 언어모델링&lt;a href="#calm-%ed%86%a0%ed%81%b0-by-%ed%86%a0%ed%81%b0-%eb%b3%91%eb%aa%a9%ec%9d%84-%ec%97%b0%ec%86%8d-%eb%b2%a1%ed%84%b0-by-%eb%b2%a1%ed%84%b0%eb%a1%9c-%ec%9a%b0%ed%9a%8c%ed%95%98%eb%8a%94-likelihood-free-%ec%96%b8%ec%96%b4%eb%aa%a8%eb%8d%b8%eb%a7%81" class="heading-anchor" aria-label="이 섹션에 대한 링크"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CALM&lt;/strong&gt; (Continuous Autoregressive Language Models) 은 (K=4) (tokens/step) 단위로 토큰을 연속 잠재벡터로 압축한 뒤 next-vector를 AR로 생성해, &lt;strong&gt;유사한 품질(BrierLM)&lt;/strong&gt; 근처에서 학습 FLOPs와 추론 FLOPs/token을 동시에 낮추는 “성능–컴퓨트 프런티어 이동”을 주장한다. (근거: §7.2, Tab.1)&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>